cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use PyEGRET, please cite it as below, and also cite the WRTDS method
  and the EGRET and EGRETci R packages it translates (listed under references, and in
  NOTICE.md).
title: "PyEGRET: a Python translation of the USGS EGRET R package and the WRTDS method"
abstract: >-
  PyEGRET translates the USGS R package EGRET (Exploration and Graphics for
  RivEr Trends) into Python: Weighted Regressions on Time, Discharge, and
  Season (WRTDS), flow normalization including the generalized form,
  WRTDS-Kalman, trend decomposition (runPairs, runGroups, runSeries),
  streamflow trend analysis, the EGRET plots, and the bootstrap uncertainty
  of EGRETci. It is validated against
  results computed by R EGRET itself.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mulukutla
    given-names: Gopal
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-29"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gopalam/PyEGRET"
url: "https://github.com/gopalam/PyEGRET"
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - hydrology
  - water quality
  - WRTDS
  - EGRET
  - trend analysis
  - flow normalization
